The requirements of \projectname{} were derived from three complementary sources:
\begin{itemize}
    \item the business objective of creating a distributed customer-data foundation under the broader \initiative{} vision;
    \item the engineering need to ingest, store, process, validate, orchestrate, expose, and monitor heterogeneous customer-related datasets;
    \item the operational reality of a lightweight academic multi-node environment with security hardening requirements.
\end{itemize}

As a result, the chapter does not present abstract requirements in isolation. Each requirement is directly connected to an implemented capability of the platform and to the final distributed deployment model.

The functional scope of the platform is centered on the end-to-end lifecycle of customer-related data, from ingestion to governed analytical access. The most important functional requirements are summarized in Table~\ref{tab:chapter4-functional-part1} and Table~\ref{tab:chapter4-functional-part2}.

\begin{table}[!htbp]
    \centering
    \footnotesize
    \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.16}
    \arrayrulecolor{tablelineblue}
    \rowcolors{2}{tablebodyblue}{white}
    \begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{|L{1.3cm}|Y|Y|}
        \hline
        \rowcolor{tableheaderblue}
        \textcolor{white}{\textbf{ID}} & \textcolor{white}{\textbf{Functional requirement}} & \textcolor{white}{\textbf{Technical acceptance criterion}} \\
        \hline
        FR-1 & Ingest heterogeneous customer-related datasets through a structured pipeline. & The platform accepts the active Client 1 datasets and routes them through the defined ingestion workflow without manual reshaping of the overall process. \\
        \hline
        FR-2 & Provide topic-based transport for reproducible raw data movement. & Kafka topics are created, used, and reset through controlled pipeline operations, with visible topic-based message flow. \\
        \hline
        FR-3 & Persist replayable raw data in a distributed bronze landing zone. & HDFS stores bronze artifacts in a durable, distributed structure that can be re-read by downstream Spark processing stages. \\
        \hline
        FR-4 & Load bronze data into governed raw lakehouse tables. & Spark reads the persisted bronze files and writes structured raw tables registered in the lakehouse layer. \\
        \hline
        FR-5 & Centralize analytical metadata for table discovery and reuse. & Hive Metastore exposes the table definitions required for downstream engines to identify and access the lakehouse objects. \\
        \hline
    \end{tabularx}
    \caption{Primary functional requirements of the platform, part 1}

\end{table}

\begin{table}[!htbp]
    \centering
    \footnotesize
    \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.16}
    \arrayrulecolor{tablelineblue}
    \rowcolors{2}{tablebodyblue}{white}
    \begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{|L{1.3cm}|Y|Y|}
        \hline
        \rowcolor{tableheaderblue}
        \textcolor{white}{\textbf{ID}} & \textcolor{white}{\textbf{Functional requirement}} & \textcolor{white}{\textbf{Technical acceptance criterion}} \\
        \hline
        FR-6 & Provide interactive SQL access for analytical exploration. & Trino executes catalog, schema, row-count, and representative analytical queries over governed lakehouse tables. \\
        \hline
        FR-7 & Support layered transformations from raw to curated analytical outputs. & dbt-spark runs declared transformation models and preserves dependency-aware model execution. \\
        \hline
        FR-8 & Apply lightweight data quality validation and persist validation evidence. & Great Expectations checks structural and semantic rules and records validation artifacts for the controlled datasets. \\
        \hline
        FR-9 & Orchestrate the operational sequence of the data platform. & Airflow executes environment reset, readiness, ingestion, and validation DAGs with visible task state and run history. \\
        \hline
        FR-10 & Expose infrastructure and pipeline observability signals. & Prometheus scrapes the configured endpoints and Grafana displays service-readiness and pipeline-oriented monitoring indicators. \\
        \hline
    \end{tabularx}
    \caption{Primary functional requirements of the platform, part 2}

\end{table}
\FloatBarrier

